  "releaseNotes": "Sensitive data protection. BREAKING DEFAULT: SQL parameter values and HTTP headers (incoming and outgoing) are no longer captured unless RequestTelemetryMiddlewareOptions.EnableSensitiveLogging is true. New MaskedHeaderNames and MaskedParameterNames options (case-insensitive, '*' wildcard) replace matching header, query string and SQL parameter values with ***; both start from DefaultMaskedHeaderNames/DefaultMaskedParameterNames (*Authorization*, Cookie, *code*, *pass*, *client*, *secret*, *subscription*, *token*, *key*, plus sig for parameters), which an application can extend or replace. Query string values in request and outgoing HTTP URLs are always masked. Masking uses allocation-free span matching (no Regex); an unmasked URL is returned as the same instance. New TelemetryManager.IsEnabled (default true): set it to false before UseRequestTelemetry to turn telemetry off completely - no listeners or middleware are registered and TrackAsync, TimelineItemContext and AddTimelineItem do nothing.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "verbatimVersion": "1.5.0",
